[{:db/id "q-104927/selection/678e76c0718c8f6d775be49733d300b744bb41c96b6292bfb11c3a90f0aeff4b" :answer/id #uuid "a11abc27-5080-5fcc-bd3e-d58e027e4b4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104927/selection/4fc89029b16c70af35f475f550da5738394df67b708fd35ae83fad2c0290f56d" :answer/id #uuid "6c97060c-5797-5ba2-a9c6-a3c5dfb80565" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104927/selection/563d03d24693be43524b2acd69d120356a5966d5b5c9d17338190c5334a6923a" :answer/id #uuid "b445e306-35e7-59bd-b34a-2e1dd542366e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104927/selection/82c5955bf83bbe4655fa8f4b9c80de880e9cec9b4ebea9c14fb99107a4eb8e08" :answer/id #uuid "3b81837e-d514-5381-a4a5-9da5c5ced503" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104927/selection/41101cfc1909920f60a24f42d1077e9193708f094690721673c626f74cd159e4" :answer/id #uuid "c0fc551e-2e2c-5b7b-a0db-f4a834e6e687" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104927/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "af11f1e1-dbb3-5edd-b401-15dd37d6c964" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104927/selection/41101cfc1909920f60a24f42d1077e9193708f094690721673c626f74cd159e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-104927/selection/678e76c0718c8f6d775be49733d300b744bb41c96b6292bfb11c3a90f0aeff4b" "q-104927/selection/4fc89029b16c70af35f475f550da5738394df67b708fd35ae83fad2c0290f56d" "q-104927/selection/563d03d24693be43524b2acd69d120356a5966d5b5c9d17338190c5334a6923a" "q-104927/selection/82c5955bf83bbe4655fa8f4b9c80de880e9cec9b4ebea9c14fb99107a4eb8e08" "q-104927/selection/41101cfc1909920f60a24f42d1077e9193708f094690721673c626f74cd159e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104927" :question/id #uuid "36779e87-7605-5095-bb25-fa2df5619013" :question/math-academy-id "q-104927" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t)={t}^{2}+3t-2$ onto the subspace spanned by $q(t)=2t-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{q(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)=\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}\\,+\\,3t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,+\\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,3t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\,+\\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,3t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot (2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =16+4 \\\\  & =20,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),q(t)⟩ & =q(-1)q(-1)+q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=-1}\\,\\,\\,+(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=0}\\,\\,\\,+(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1}\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,(2t\\,-\\,2){|}_{t=1} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =16+4+0 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{20}\\cdot (2t-2) \\\\  & =2t-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104927/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df300955-830a-5347-9aeb-2b2b25f865c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104927"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-104944"] :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $1$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t)=-3t-2$ onto the subspace spanned by the polynomial $q(t)=t.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{q(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)=\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(-3t-2){|}_{0}\\cdot (t){|}_{0}+(-3t-2){|}_{1}\\cdot (t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 0+(-5)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0-5 \\\\  & =-5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),q(t)⟩ & =q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(t){|}_{0}\\cdot (t){|}_{0}+(t){|}_{1}\\cdot (t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{1}\\cdot t \\\\  & =-5t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-98694"] :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $f(t)=2{t}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by $g(t)=6t-3.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $f(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{g(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t)=\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{t}^{2}\\cdot (6t-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(12{t}^{3}-6{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[3{t}^{4}-2{t}^{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(3-2)-0 \\\\  & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6t-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{t}^{2}-36t+9)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[12{t}^{3}-18{t}^{2}+9t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(12-18+9)-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (6t-3) \\\\  & =2t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-104936/selection/5586b4839b175d9e9dd5a069e42d957654567688da5df23e3a5021a2497e33f6" :answer/id #uuid "bf4bea6d-2e30-52e5-98e7-edf4e55f676a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{t}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104936/selection/87874912d3fa89ed08402be53c9c9e441d69cc7480cb3848269e0c5cd0d57ccc" :answer/id #uuid "f1d3a344-c8f5-5ce9-adef-0e806fe360da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{t}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104936/selection/d03ee7559172352af651a427c95f211a1822d321bd666c363fbe7fc3996a605d" :answer/id #uuid "4160c9de-5b36-54e8-8e64-f5625de91ecc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{t}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104936/selection/6871257517aa672552abac54ca0aad2864b52af0980c48990f327138524aa2b4" :answer/id #uuid "e5f12df4-cc65-5436-a026-cff66d1f218c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10{t}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104936/selection/d1a62ddd3420809b9f299b2c479611938da7397f536baa38b0f67ae81becc750" :answer/id #uuid "869904bb-d61b-50d8-b430-2b803f29a800" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{t}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104936/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ac5d6b5-53c6-5ba2-a77b-e4b63d9f3cc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104936/selection/6871257517aa672552abac54ca0aad2864b52af0980c48990f327138524aa2b4" :answer-field/choices ["q-104936/selection/5586b4839b175d9e9dd5a069e42d957654567688da5df23e3a5021a2497e33f6" "q-104936/selection/87874912d3fa89ed08402be53c9c9e441d69cc7480cb3848269e0c5cd0d57ccc" "q-104936/selection/d03ee7559172352af651a427c95f211a1822d321bd666c363fbe7fc3996a605d" "q-104936/selection/6871257517aa672552abac54ca0aad2864b52af0980c48990f327138524aa2b4" "q-104936/selection/d1a62ddd3420809b9f299b2c479611938da7397f536baa38b0f67ae81becc750"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104936" :question/id #uuid "4a15e7fe-ea3e-5b2e-bcc2-2e4f7497493e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104936" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-1,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[-1,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $f(t)={t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}+2$ onto the subspace spanned by $g(t)=5{t}^{2}+1.$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $f(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{g(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t)=\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}+2)\\cdot (5{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(5{t}^{5}+50{t}^{4}+{t}^{3}+20{t}^{2}+2)\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{6}{t}^{6}+10{t}^{5}+\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{20}{3}{t}^{3}+2t]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{6}+10+\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{20}{3}+2)-(\\frac{5}{6}-10+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{20}{3}-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{112}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(5{t}^{2}+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(25{t}^{4}+10{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[5{t}^{5}+\\frac{10}{3}{t}^{3}+t]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(5+\\frac{10}{3}+1)-(-5-\\frac{10}{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{112}{3})}{(\\frac{56}{3})}\\cdot (5{t}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =2(5{t}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =10{t}^{2}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104936/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df300955-830a-5347-9aeb-2b2b25f865c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104936"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105411/selection/7657de90a7e2e0b77103c1b63e5fe52f9a61ea3214472ad6a1973b64a513d64a" :answer/id #uuid "9b210915-ee27-5e70-b099-869927e7d6b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{t}^{2}-3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105411/selection/49e1ed81d72828598de4aee43893055462859fa04509facee342e49253ace320" :answer/id #uuid "910ea412-2e8c-5c6a-9d65-8ed12acaec38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105411/selection/758b94178b21f275742a3726fc22756331d650d8dd18f5e32de008611615a9e7" :answer/id #uuid "e97a43e7-eebe-5779-a417-fe97395b9373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}+7t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105411/selection/dc81c62a29668c3af12d8da2cd615ac681628902a2afd889636eebad30458d2d" :answer/id #uuid "f6f4bb00-1a0d-59c7-b790-b9fea275a974" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{t}^{2}-7t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105411/selection/c4bdf574ee47ecb43bb150c8b3deba04082696447a43778a66c09df7e103fd5f" :answer/id #uuid "509c67cd-a6bd-559a-8a27-c6ce696298d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}+7t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105411/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6227f66-2d7c-5d0e-86b6-829436964782" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105411/selection/c4bdf574ee47ecb43bb150c8b3deba04082696447a43778a66c09df7e103fd5f" :answer-field/choices ["q-105411/selection/7657de90a7e2e0b77103c1b63e5fe52f9a61ea3214472ad6a1973b64a513d64a" "q-105411/selection/49e1ed81d72828598de4aee43893055462859fa04509facee342e49253ace320" "q-105411/selection/758b94178b21f275742a3726fc22756331d650d8dd18f5e32de008611615a9e7" "q-105411/selection/dc81c62a29668c3af12d8da2cd615ac681628902a2afd889636eebad30458d2d" "q-105411/selection/c4bdf574ee47ecb43bb150c8b3deba04082696447a43778a66c09df7e103fd5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105411" :question/id #uuid "0728cec7-8cb7-5ad9-ad8b-8c973bf6c1d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-105411" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $2,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}-t,\\,q(t)=7t-3\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t)}$ equals $2{t}^{2}+2t.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)=2{t}^{2}+2t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t)=\\frac{⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{p}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =q(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+q(0){p}_{2}(0)+q(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =(7t\\,-\\,3){|}_{-1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,-\\,t){|}_{-1}+(7t\\,-\\,3){|}_{0}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,-\\,t){|}_{0}+(7t\\,-\\,3){|}_{1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,-\\,t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-10)\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-20,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={p}_{2}(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+{p}_{2}(0){p}_{2}(0)+{p}_{2}(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-t)^{2}{|}_{-1}+({t}^{2}-t)^{2}{|}_{0}+({t}^{2}-t)^{2}{|}_{1} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) & =\\frac{-20}{4}\\cdot ({t}^{2}-t)=-5{t}^{2}+5t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}+2t+(-5{t}^{2}+5t) \\\\  & =-3{t}^{2}+7t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105411/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39692b40-7d68-5ae5-9fe1-0f8b0b2e0d77"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105411"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105186/selection/8450a6a7e5b8aa0b284043dc39dbf5e29a7c7f6efd703566fe7b94ebba6f70da" :answer/id #uuid "782761c3-0230-5927-92c9-6092c0f6331a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105186/selection/1ad27eb350b35c3e5cdeb8aac47c3ce7a0dabb480833c65cb041e9694c50a787" :answer/id #uuid "9b40a754-0f6e-5e0a-980a-92d512cf6021" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105186/selection/97c51be3e05f2374119ac39fd0a42a3c8ef67110fb54dd567fd5a30ec2869d7a" :answer/id #uuid "4c1fb457-99a2-5811-ab3f-f53b0b6a937b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105186/selection/0d6f51ea6b0170de83412091e0e98b43c41369789414fcec4a5a29c484a4693c" :answer/id #uuid "2d812a72-abfd-5dbf-a6c4-f3c68ae93b4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105186/selection/37e7d3213aea08fb68f2a1f14c6fcc1fc152125f6f4d94a6bbaf3b4e0ec55d7d" :answer/id #uuid "dc38c325-9193-588f-a5e8-672bfee83e48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105186/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "883692f4-25f5-546c-8689-b4b858bc140a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105186/selection/0d6f51ea6b0170de83412091e0e98b43c41369789414fcec4a5a29c484a4693c" :answer-field/choices ["q-105186/selection/8450a6a7e5b8aa0b284043dc39dbf5e29a7c7f6efd703566fe7b94ebba6f70da" "q-105186/selection/1ad27eb350b35c3e5cdeb8aac47c3ce7a0dabb480833c65cb041e9694c50a787" "q-105186/selection/97c51be3e05f2374119ac39fd0a42a3c8ef67110fb54dd567fd5a30ec2869d7a" "q-105186/selection/0d6f51ea6b0170de83412091e0e98b43c41369789414fcec4a5a29c484a4693c" "q-105186/selection/37e7d3213aea08fb68f2a1f14c6fcc1fc152125f6f4d94a6bbaf3b4e0ec55d7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105186" :question/id #uuid "e2080217-de30-5eca-8115-9c201cc1f5f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-105186" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the vector space of continuous functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=2,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,g(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+6\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t)}$ equals $6.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)=6,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{f}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(t){f}_{2}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+6)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+6{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ is an odd function, while $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is even. Hence, their product $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ must be an odd function. Now, since we have integrals over the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ which is symmetric about the origin, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩ & =-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) & =\\frac{-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t}{⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =\\frac{-2{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =6-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-105186/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39692b40-7d68-5ae5-9fe1-0f8b0b2e0d77"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105186"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105511/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer/id #uuid "29268b14-9dad-566d-b2ea-e4df7b155fb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105511/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "182ac55b-0ba9-575f-ad58-99e9ef0dc4b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105511/selection/ed480161c278cf263b7506697b7b27c19b2594926ada6527945331e6eb5a4b3b" :answer/id #uuid "c430b1e2-2ca0-5bd2-94fa-688b72e05c6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105511/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "08cec776-a982-5d49-b7ad-f5375fe18bcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105511/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer/id #uuid "4fcdcdfe-a472-5d23-b3de-f14dbecc7163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105511/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d20b91ad-bc8b-5f7a-aa38-b7f372af9dfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105511/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" :answer-field/choices ["q-105511/selection/7346ebe1e5d722acf040262ae8e6e53d26ca80a32da08982328df7eef98b7372" "q-105511/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-105511/selection/ed480161c278cf263b7506697b7b27c19b2594926ada6527945331e6eb5a4b3b" "q-105511/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-105511/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105511" :question/id #uuid "b94e9d5c-1cb0-573a-aa02-9ccad478730f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105511" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=7t$ and the subspace spanned by $g(t)=t-2$ with respect to the inner product." :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $f(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{g(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\int }_{0}^{1}7t\\cdot (t-2)\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot (t-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(7{t}^{2}-14t)\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}-4t+4)\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot (t-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{[\\frac{7}{3}{t}^{3}-7{t}^{2}]_{0}^{1}}{[\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+4t]_{0}^{1}}\\cdot (t-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{14}{3})}{(\\frac{7}{3})}\\cdot (t-2) \\\\  & =-2t+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distance between $f(t)=7t$ and the subspace spanned by $g(t)=t-2$ with respect to our inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖7t-(-2t+4)‖ \\\\  & =‖9t-4‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨9t-4,9t-4⟩}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨9t-4,9t-4⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9t-4)\\cdot (9t-4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9t-4)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(81{t}^{2}-72t+16)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(27{t}^{3}-36{t}^{2}+16)\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{7}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105511/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25e84fac-02c3-5111-98b3-bc67fe1ec9ab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105511"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
